<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Strasbourg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">357</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Argentoratum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Strasbourg, or Argentoratum, was fought in August 357 near Strasbourg between a Roman army under the Caesar Julian and a coalition of Alemannic kings led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chnodomar">Chnodomar</a> and his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serapio">Serapio</a>. Julian's roughly 13,000 men defeated a force that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ammianus-marcellinus">Ammianus Marcellinus</a> put at some 35,000; Chnodomar was captured and sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. The victory restored Roman control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> frontier and made Julian's reputation.</p></div>
